{# NESTED must_match_fields — the case the generated CRD could not express until
   crdgen was fixed.

   The proto type is google.protobuf.Struct and the field's own doc comment promises
   "strings, numbers, booleans, and nested fields". crdgen used to emit
   `additionalProperties: true` for Struct (schemagen.go, the .google.protobuf.Struct
   case), i.e. "any key allowed, values unspecified" — and a value with NO schema has no
   known sub-fields, so the API server pruned everything one level down. Strict clients
   saw that as a rejection:

     unknown field "spec.generic_oidc.must_match_fields.nested.deep"

   while non-strict ones silently stored `nested: {}` — which degrades this matcher to a
   mere existence check. crdgen now emits x-kubernetes-preserve-unknown-fields instead
   (as it already did for the Labels custom type just above that case), so the whole
   tree survives.

   This CR is the REGRESSION GUARD for that fix. The op-agent-oknested /
   op-agent-badnested pair then proves the nested rule is ENFORCED rather than merely
   stored — precisely the failure the pruned-to-`{}` case would otherwise hide. #}
apiVersion: resources.teleport.dev/v2
kind: TeleportProvisionToken
metadata:
  name: op-oidc-nested
  namespace: teleport
spec:
  roles: [Node]
  join_method: generic_oidc
  generic_oidc:
    issuer: "https://oidc.{{ lab_domain }}:8443"
    audience: "{{ fqdn }}/generic-oidc"
    must_match_fields:
      org: ethernet-fyi
      nested:
        deep: {{ nested_value }}
    allow_any:
      - conditions:
          - attribute: sub
            eq: {value: "{{ oidc_subject }}"}
